      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T04:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This customizer class is not clear. Why do you need a customizer class? All the attributes that are being added to the packet in this commit are standard Radius attributes. This customizer class is not desirable.\nIt is also not good practice to provide a name of a class as a part of the configuration.",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_de02e30a",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/AaaConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000097
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T18:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that all the attributes that are being added to the packet are standard RADIUS attributes. But there are certain things which are very specific to the operator (for example as you pointed above that the AccessDeviceName could be used as the NAS Identifier). These things are operator or setup specific and should go into the customizer class for that particular operator/setup. Also the operator might not want to disclose all these details about it\u0027s network in the open source, so these customizer files could be kept away.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_dec0a32c",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_beddef16",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/AaaConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T04:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not the responsibility of the AAA app to keep the port to s/c tag bindings. It is the responsibility of \"OLT\" app. \nIs it not desirable for the operator to add every RG\u0027s MAC into ONOS. Also note that the AAA app is only support port-based-authentication(as per AT\u0026T requirement).\n \nComments on the attributes added in bindings:\na) NAS-Port-Id : This should be derived from the OF port, i.e. the \"portName\" of the OF port (which will be UNI port in the case of OLT) that is being authenticated. NAS-Port-Id attribute is used by the Radius server to identify the UNI port that is being authenticated. OpenFlow has a ability to learn the PortName dynamically for every OF Port from the device. Why not use that? \nAlso with your approach, if the RG is changed, you need to delete and add the binding for the new MAC which is inconvenient. The NAS-Port-Id attribute is used to uniquely identify the subscriber port(i.e. the UNI port on the RG) and not the RG. \nSame \"DeviceName\" and \"PortName\" scheme can be used by L2 DHCP Relay as well (Refer below to AT\u0026T\u0027s requirement in https://wiki.opencord.org/download/attachments/1966449/EPIC_3_SDN.pdf?version\u003d1\u0026modificationDate\u003d1478138202209\u0026api\u003dv2)\n3.2.1.44 The NAS-Port-Id in the RADIUS request shall have the same format as the circuit-id added by the OLT layer2 DHCP relay agent in the Option 82 Agent Circuit-id field. It shall contains the same AID, but with no TID(node identifier). L2940\nb) S \u0026 C tags: As mentioned earlier, it is not desirable that these are configured into AAA app. These need to be configured to OLT app directly. There could be multiple C-tags per in future.",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_99792596",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/AaaConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000097
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T18:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed on the S\u0026C tags, they should not be in the AAA App. You can ignore for the moment, I will remove them. Regarding the NAS-Port-Id, yes the idea of using it from the Of Port Name is good, but even it that case it needs to be configured in voltha which would populate it. In this case the port is not a physical port and it is not guaranteed (unless the voltha adapters for the OLT are written in such a way) that the same ONU/RG will always have the name port number across reboots, so using the RG of the MAC might also be an option. In my opinion we should have the NAS-Port-Id configurable for each RG/ONU or read from the portName of OF port, but this could be done in the customization file as it\u0027s not a generic approach.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_beddef16",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
