        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T04:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "deleteStateMachineMappings(StateMachine machine) - This is called even in the case when the session is authorized and session Id for an authorized session is deleted here. If a EAPOL_LOGOFF is received from the supplicant, how to send ACCESS_REJECT to the Radius Server, since the sessionId is no longer present? Similarly whenever RE-AUTHENTICATION is implemented, the session Id will be needed as well.",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_b99bc9c8",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/StateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000097
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T18:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, this is a bug and the entry from the sessionIdMap should not be deleted. Only the entries from the identifierMap need to be cleared off.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_9e090b98",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_7efe376d",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/StateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T04:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like you changed the sessionId allocation mechanism. It would be better to look at pending changes from other vendors before merging to see which one need to be used.",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_99a005f6",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/StateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000097
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T18:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No we have not changed the sessionId allocation; rather we have changed the identifier allocation mechanism. With the old way of allocating identifiers (using the same value for all the RADIUS messages for an authentication sequence) we saw the RADIUS server indicating duplicate identifiers.\nFrom RFC 2865:\n\"The Identifier field is one octet, and aids in matching requests and replies.  The RADIUS server can detect a duplicate request if it has the same client source IP address and source UDP port and Identifier within a short span of time.\"",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_7efe376d",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_5e037373",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/aaa/StateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-08T04:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "deleteStateMachineMappings(StateMachine machine) - The session Id for an authorized session is deleted here. If a EAPOL_LOGOFF is received from the supplicant, how to send ACCESS_REJECT to the Radius Server, since the sessionId is no longer present? Similarly whenever RE-AUTHENTICATION is implemented, the session Id will be needed as well.",
      "revId": "c74cbc43011bf331e3260357cf4236f4346eae74",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
